In article <1992Aug5.050602.22155@usenet.ins.cwru.edu> jwk3@po.CWRU.Edu (John W. Kale) writes:
>For example, a Valkyrie can zap herself
>with a wand of speed (one speedup), wear speed boots (two speedups),
>and then earn the speed intrinsic by advancing to experience level
>seven (for a whopping three speedups). How fast is the resulting 
>character, really? Does some kind source-code-owning person know?

I believe I count as a source-code-owning person, so I think I'll answer this.
Speed that you get from speed boots or a potion happens once every other move.
Intrinsic speed, whether from being a Valkyrie, or zapping yourself, happens
occasionally, not every other move.  There are only these two levels.
